  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A9 (cut sizes). Two representation classes stay explicit. X76's and X78's cut sizes count the edges of the graph with one end in A and the other outside; after M1 their bodies convert to the new GTBase.common.cut_size A := #|[set e in E(G) | ~~ [disjoint e & A] && ~~ (e \\subset A)]|. X209's cut size counts the members of an ARBITRARY supplied family that are not monochromatic under an arbitrary supplied ordinal colouring; it now unfolds to the graph-free GTBase.monochromatic.non_monochromatic_count, and its cut-edge test x209_cut_edge to C8's ~~ monochromatic_on (non_monochromatic_onP, a proved equality). No uniformity, nonemptiness, positivity or palette premise is added. Three statements are affected (X76, X78, X209) through X209's three chains (is_max_r_cut, scaled_excess, is_min_scaled_excess).",
    "",
    "X209 defect, preserved: x209_is_min_scaled_excess binds a fresh T' but types E' over the OUTER carrier T, so T' is unused; the frozen chain keeps it verbatim and the row is not repaired. History: A7's X76/X78 per-row copies and Originals and A5's X78 snapshot call the live cut sizes and are documented below. X76Original and X78Original are pre-M1: cut sizes at 061154c over M1's frozen comprehension (bridged by M1's certificates), A7's pre-M1 counts and, for X78, A5's frozen containment. Natural subtraction, expected denominators, quantifier order, the whole excess function, statuses and doc blocks are unchanged."
  ],
